{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01Bdr6Z2psZrrCLcBa4ZB4Ei","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Anchor is a personal productivity and R&D control system built for J.C. Liechty. Here's what it is, grounded in the project docs:\n\n- **A single-folder, markdown-backed task/productivity system.** Everything lives in `C:\\dev\\Anchor` â€” no database, no syncing, no external dependencies (Python stdlib only, with one declared exception). Plain markdown files (`DASHBOARD.md`, `PROJECTS.md`, `INBOX.md`, per-domain files) are the source of truth, and all files stay accessible from any CLI/editor.\n\n- **It ships a self-contained local web app â€” `anchor_gui.py`** (the one declared deliverable). It's a stdlib HTTP server that renders the full dashboard, writes directly back to the markdown files, and runs persistently in the background as the NSSM Windows service `anchor` bound to `http://localhost:8777` on host PUTER/gwl-server.\n\n- **A task lifecycle engine + CLI mirror.** Tasks move through Active â†’ Done â†’ Cancelled â†’ Saved-for-Later â†’ Restored, with a matching `anchor.py` command-line tool that shares the same markdown format and also generates a static `dashboard.html`.\n\n- **An \"R&D Control Surface\" for trio-driven project work** (the major recent build), evolved across three versions. It turns each project's window into a \"Mission Control\" cockpit for the **researchPrime â†’ Crucible â†’ Foreman** trio, with per-lane session tiles, honest status lights (green/amber/red/grey), cached/validated AI summaries, and a Grass-Catchers idea lane.\n\n- **v3 \"Mission Control\" adds real interactive terminals.** Per-session ConPTY terminals (the lone `pywinpty` native-dependency exception, lazy-loaded), git-worktree isolation per session, a stacking xterm.js window manager, in-place expandable summaries, stage handoffs, a runnable deliverable preview (ephemeral port hard-guarded â‰  8777), and Ghost World Labs branding. Built, all 10 waves green, merged to master 2026-06-12.\n\n- **It's self-testing.** A daily 5 AM health check parses every markdown file, boots a throwaway server, exercises every endpoint and the full v2 + v3 R&D surfaces (fully stubbed â€” never live `claude`/ConPTY), and writes a dated report.\n\nOne note on current state: you're on branch `foreman/rnd-surface-v4` with a **v4 redesign** in flight (per memory: branding mockups + project-window paradigms + a proven ConPTYÃ—WSÃ—xterm harness, awaiting your paradigm pick) â€” so the cockpit/North-Star anchors quoted above describe the *v4 target*, not yet a merged surface."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4412,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":41003,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"39e76d86-af9d-44f7-b303-f2deb2ae4c9a","uuid":"17cfe70b-b040-4255-83d7-bebc339609fc","request_id":"req_011CbykVAMZcdzsyA7hEPEzG"}
